ity of E. coli, Enterobacter, Klebsiella, and Proteus species.\nL24: Secondary ChEBI ID  | CHEBI:7456\nL25: Last Modified  | 19 June 2017\nL26: Downloads  | 【14†Molfile】\nL27: On this page\nL28: \nL29:   * 【15†Intro】\nL30:   * 【16†Roles Classification】\nL31:   * 【17†Ontology】\nL32:   * 【18†Names】\nL33:   * 【19†Manual Xrefs】\nL34:   * 【20†Registry Numbers】\nL35:   * 【21†Citations】\nL36: \nL37: Formula  | C12H12N2O3\nL38: Net Charge  | 0\nL39: Average Mass  | 232.239\nL40: Monoisotopic Mass  | 232.08479\nL41: SMILES  | CCn1cc(C(=O)O)c(=O)c2ccc(C)nc21\nL42: InChI  | InChI=1S/C12H12N2O3/c1-3-14-6-9(12(16)17)10(15)8-5-4-7(2)13-11(8)14/h4-6H,3H2,1-2H3,(H,16,17)\nL43: InChIKey  | MHWLWQUZZRMNGJ-UHFFFAOYSA-N\nL44: \nL45: Wikipedia\nL46: ---\nL47: \nL48: Roles Classification\nL49: ---\nL50: 【22†Chemical Role:】  | 【23†Bronsted acid】  A molecular entity capable of donating a hydron to an acceptor (Brønsted base).\nL51: 【24†Biological Roles:】  | 【25†antibacterial drug】  A drug used to treat or prevent bacterial infections.【26†DNA synthesis inhibitor】  Any substance that inhibits the synthesis of DNA.【27†antibacterial agent】  A substance (or active part thereof) that kills or slows the growth of bacteria.【28†antimicrobial agent】  A substance that kills or slows the growth of microorganisms, including bacteria, viruses, fungi and protozoans.【28†antimicrobial agent】  A substance that kills or slows the growth of microorganisms, including bacteria, viruses, fungi and protozoans.【28†antimicrobial agent】  A substance that kills or slows the growth of microorganisms, including bacteria, viruses, fungi and protozoans.【28†antimicrobial agent】  A substance that kills or slows the growth of microorganisms, including bacteria, viruses, fungi and protozoans.\nL52: 【29†Application:】  | 【25†antibacterial drug】  A drug used to treat or prevent bacterial infections.\nL53: ChEBI Ontology\nL54: ---\nL55: \nL56: Text\nL57: \nL58: Tree View\nL59: \nL60: Graph View\nL61: Outgoing Relation(s)\nL62: n